==English==
{{was wotd|2020|January|27}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|iniquite}}, {{m|enm|jniquite|t=evil, wickedness, iniquity; evil act; hostility, malevolence; hostile act; a calamity, misfortune}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=iniquitẹ̄ |pos=n|id=MED22759}}</ref> from {{der|en|fro|iniquité}} (modern {{cog|fr|iniquité|t=iniquity}}), from {{der|en|la|inīquitās|t=iniquity; inequality, unfairness; inequity, injustice}}, from {{m|la|inīquus|t=unequal, uneven, unfair; disadvantageous, unfavourable; hostile, unkind; unsuitable; wicked, wrong}} + {{m|la|-itās}} (variant of {{m|la|-tās|pos=''suffix forming a {{glossary|noun}} indicating a state of being''}}). ''Inīquus'' is derived from {{m|la|in-|pos=''prefix meaning ‘not’''}} + {{m|la|aequus|t=equal; fair, impartial, just}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=96048|date=1900|nodot=yes}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref> Compare {{m|en|inequity}}.

